<title>HUNGARY: COMMERZBANK HUNGARY UNIT BOOSTS H1 PROFITS.</title>
<headline>COMMERZBANK HUNGARY UNIT BOOSTS H1 PROFITS.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					Jan-June 1997     Jan-June 1996</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			735     vs	  520</p>
<p>    After-tax profit		    662     vs	  441</p>
<p>    Net interest income	     1,073     vs	  746</p>
<p>	 Interest revenue	     3,672     vs	3,486</p>
<p>	 Interest expenditure	 2,599     vs	2,740</p>
<p>    Fee revenue			   271     vs	  284</p>
<p>    Interbank lendings	     41,626     vs     26,439</p>
<p>    Lendings to clients	    23,431     vs     19,065</p>
<p>    Deposits from banks	    60,037     vs     46,514</p>
<p>    Deposits from clients	  14,134     vs     10,572</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total	    87,564     vs     65,177</p>
<p>    Capital adequacy ratio (pct) 58.29	vs     31.25 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Commerzbank (Budapest) Rt is the subsidiary of Germany's Commerzbank AG</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
